# `dig` returns whatever its last step finds, False included: only Null is
# special, and only as a structure still to be indexed. Subtle because False
# is falsy like Null, yet must come back as itself rather than as Null.
#= {result: [false, 0, ''], inputs: {data: {a: {b: false}, n: [0], s: {t: ''}}}}
[dig(data, 'a', 'b'), dig(data, 'n', 0), dig(data, 's', 't')]
